Subject: Dedicated threaded handlers for the measured cold opcodes

What this does
  Dedicated threaded handlers for the cold opcodes.

Why we need it
  `regvm_t_cold` costs two tail calls plus the `regvm_exec_one` switch per dispatch.

What it adds
  Handlers for load_i32, add/sub_imm_s, add/sub_imm_self_s, object_template, array_from, put_global, get_length, put_element, object_fill, get_arg_el, local_rmw_branch, tail_call, tail_call_method; `tools/regvm/threadcover.py`; also fixes the `sub_imm` overflow fallback adding instead of subtracting.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
